(window.RW_DISPLAY = window.RW_DISPLAY || {})["test05_1A"] = [{"id":"bcc91b1e","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"The spacecraft OSIRIS-REx briefly made contact with the asteroid 101955 Bennu in 2020. NASA scientist Daniella DellaGiustina reports that despite facing the unexpected obstacle of a surface mostly covered in boulders, OSIRIS-REx successfully ______ a sample of the surface, gathering pieces of it to bring back to Earth.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The spacecraft OSIRIS-REx briefly made contact with the asteroid 101955 Bennu in 2020. NASA scientist Daniella DellaGiustina reports that","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"despite facing the unexpected obstacle of a surface mostly covered in boulders, OSIRIS-REx successfully ______ a sample of the surface,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"gathering pieces of it to bring back to Earth.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["attached","collected","followed","replaced"]},{"id":"809addda","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"The following text is from Ameen Rihani’s 1921 poem “The Wanderer.” I wander among the hills of alien lands Where Nature her prerogative resigns To Man; where Comfort in her shack reclines And all the arts and sciences commands. But in my soul The eastern billows roll — I hear the voices of my native strands.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The following text is from Ameen Rihani’s 1921 poem “The Wanderer.”","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"I wander among the hills of alien lands","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Where Nature her prerogative resigns","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"To Man; where Comfort in her shack reclines","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"And all the arts and sciences commands.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"But in my soul","indent":3},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"The eastern billows roll—","indent":3},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"I hear the voices of my native strands.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined lines in the text as a whole?","choices":["It establishes that the speaker’s enthusiasm about current travels conflicts with the growing urge to return home.","It illustrates the speaker’s uncertainty about maintaining strong links with relatives in distant places.","It conveys the speaker’s sense of feeling a pull toward home while traveling in an unfamiliar place.","It reveals that upon returning after an extended absence, the speaker longs for the way a location once felt."],"underline":null,"underline_segments":["But in my soul","The eastern billows roll—","I hear the voices of my native strands."]},{"id":"757077f9","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"During a 2014 archaeological dig in Spain, Vicente Lull and his team uncovered the skeleton of a woman from El Algar, an Early Bronze Age society, buried with valuable objects signaling a high position of power. This finding may persuade researchers who have argued that Bronze Age societies were ruled by men to ______ that women may have also held leadership roles.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"During a 2014 archaeological dig in Spain, Vicente Lull and his team uncovered the skeleton of a woman from El Algar, an Early Bronze Age","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"society, buried with valuable objects signaling a high position of power. This finding may persuade researchers who have argued that Bronze Age","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"societies were ruled by men to ______ that women may have also held leadership roles.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["waive","concede","refute","require"]},{"id":"e1d5d5df","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"According to botanists, a viburnum plant experiencing insect damage may develop erineum — a discolored, felty growth — on its leaf blades. A ______ viburnum plant, on the other hand, will have leaves with smooth surfaces and uniformly green coloration.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["struggling","beneficial","simple","healthy"]},{"id":"617a8a10","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"Very little is known about the role nocturnal insects, such as moths, play in flower pollination because it is difficult to monitor insects at night. To address this problem, a team of scientists used time-lapse cameras to record pollinator visits to red clover all day and night. The recordings showed that while most pollinator visits were by bumblebees, one-third of visits were by moths. Additionally, flowers that were visited by both moths and bees produced more seeds than flowers that were only visited by bees.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Very little is known about the role nocturnal insects, such as moths, play in flower pollination because it is difficult to monitor insects at night. To","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"address this problem, a team of scientists used time-lapse cameras to record pollinator visits to red clover all day and night. The recordings","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"showed that while most pollinator visits were by bumblebees, one-third of visits were by moths. Additionally, flowers that were visited by both","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"moths and bees produced more seeds than flowers that were only visited by bees.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best states the function of the underlined sentence?","choices":["To describe an approach a team of scientists used to study pollinators","To question a claim scientists make about pollinators","To explain why moths prefer red clover to other flowers","To announce an unexpected research finding about red clover"],"underline":null,"underline_segments":["To","address this problem, a team of scientists used time-lapse cameras to record pollinator visits to red clover all day and night."]},{"id":"cd2ce51f","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"Like the 1945 play it reimagines — Federico García Lorca’s The House of Bernarda Alba — Marcus Gardley’s 2014 play The House That Will Not Stand prominently features women. In both plays, the all-female cast ______ an array of female characters, including a strong mother and several daughters dealing with individual struggles.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Like the 1945 play it reimagines—Federico García Lorca’s The House of Bernarda Alba—Marcus Gardley’s 2014 play The House That Will Not Stand","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"prominently features women. In both plays, the all-female cast ______ an array of female characters, including a strong mother and several","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"daughters dealing with individual struggles.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["engulfs","encourages","comprises","provokes"]},{"id":"e3f05561","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"In the 1970s, video cameras became increasingly affordable for ordinary consumers and gave Ulysses Jenkins and other artists capabilities that were previously unavailable except to television broadcasters. Jenkins recognized and took full advantage of this ______ access to powerful technology to create groundbreaking works of video art, such as Mass of Images (1978).","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["newfound","delicate","inevitable","habitual"]},{"id":"c6bd3447","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"The following text is from Virginia Woolf’s 1919 novel Night and Day. The text describes a gathering of young artists and intellectuals. One person after another rose, and, as with an ill-balanced axe, attempted to hew out his conception of art a little more clearly, and sat down with the feeling that, for some reason which he could not grasp, his strokes had gone awry. As they sat down they turned almost invariably to the person sitting next them, and rectified and continued what they had just said in public.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The following text is from Virginia Woolf’s 1919 novel Night and Day. The text describes a gathering of young artists and intellectuals.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"One person after another rose, and, as with an ill-balanced axe, attempted to hew out his conception of art a little more clearly,","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"and sat down with the feeling that, for some reason which he could not grasp, his strokes had gone awry. As they sat down they","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"turned almost invariably to the person sitting next them, and rectified and continued what they had just said in public.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined portions in the text as a whole?","choices":["To demonstrate individuals puzzlement over the reputation of a certain artwork","To highlight the physical effort involved in individuals construction of large-scale works of art","To draw attention to individuals discontent with the group’s conversation about art","To emphasize the extent of individuals struggles to articulate thoughts on art"],"underline":null,"underline_segments":["an ill-balanced axe, attempted to hew out","strokes had gone awry."]},{"id":"26ee16ba","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Hip-hop pedagogy is a form of teaching that’s gaining popularity across school subjects. It involves incorporating hip-hop and rap music into lessons as well as using hip-hop elements when teaching other subject matters. For example, Quan Neloms’s students look for college-level vocabulary and historical events in rap songs. Researchers claim that in addition to developing students’ social justice awareness, hip-hop pedagogy encourages student success by raising students’ interest and engagement.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Hip-hop pedagogy is a form of teaching that’s gaining popularity across school subjects. It involves incorporating hip-hop and rap music into","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"lessons as well as using hip-hop elements when teaching other subject matters. For example, Quan Neloms’s students look for college-level","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"vocabulary and historical events in rap songs. Researchers claim that in addition to developing students’ social justice awareness, hip-hop","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"pedagogy encourages student success by raising students’ interest and engagement.","indent":0}],"question":"Which finding, if true, would most strongly support the underlined claim?","choices":["Students tend to be more enthusiastic about rap music than they are about hip-hop music.","Students who are highly interested in social justice issues typically don’t sign up for courses that incorporate hip-hop and rap music.","Educators report that they enjoy teaching courses that involve hip-hop and rap music more than teaching courses that don’t.","Courses that incorporate hip-hop and rap music are among the courses with the highest enrollment and attendance rates."],"underline":null,"underline_segments":["hip-hop","pedagogy encourages student success by raising students’ interest and engagement."]},{"id":"8f3a200e","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Information and Ideas · Central Ideas and Details","passage":"Some astronomers searching for extraterrestrial life have proposed that atmospheric NH 3 (ammonia) can serve as a biosignature gas — an indication that a planet harbors life. Jingcheng Huang, Sara Seager, and colleagues evaluated this possibility, finding that on rocky planets, atmospheric NH 3 likely couldn’t reach detectably high levels in the absence of biological activity. But the team also found that on so-called mini- Neptunes — gas planets smaller than Neptune but with atmospheres similar to Neptune’s ’— atmospheric pressure and temperature can be high enough to produce atmospheric NH 3.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Some astronomers searching for extraterrestrial life have proposed that atmospheric NH3 (ammonia) can serve as a biosignature gas—an","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"indication that a planet harbors life. Jingcheng Huang, Sara Seager, and colleagues evaluated this possibility, finding that on rocky planets,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"atmospheric NH3 likely couldn’t reach detectably high levels in the absence of biological activity. But the team also found that on so-called mini-","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Neptunes—gas planets smaller than Neptune but with atmospheres similar to Neptune’s—atmospheric pressure and temperature can be high","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"enough to produce atmospheric NH3.","indent":0}],"question":"Based on the text, Huang, Seager, and colleagues would most likely agree with which statement about atmospheric NH ?","choices":["Its presence is more likely to indicate that a planet is a mini-Neptune than that the planet is a rocky planet that could support life.","Its absence from a planet that’s not a mini-Neptune indicates that the planet probably doesn’t have life.","It should be treated as a biosignature gas if detected in the atmosphere of a rocky planet but not if detected in the atmosphere of a mini- Neptune.","It doesn’t reliably reach high enough concentrations in the atmospheres of rocky planets or mini-Neptunes to be treated as a biosignature gas."]},{"id":"abbea24d","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"“The Mountain” is a 1914 poem by Robert Frost. In the poem,","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"“The Mountain” is a 1914 poem by Robert Frost. In the poem, the speaker visits a town next to a mountain. The speaker claims to feel protected","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"by the mountain, saying ______","indent":0}],"question":"Which quotation from “The Mountain” most effectively illustrates the claim?","choices":["“A dry ravine emerged under boughs / Into the pasture.”","“The mountain stood there to be pointed at.”","“I felt it like a wall / Behind which I was sheltered from a wind.”","“I crossed the river and swung round the mountain.”"]},{"id":"9abc3ba5","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Inferences","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Information and Ideas · Inferences","passage":"“Gestures” in painting are typically thought of as bold, expressive brushstrokes. In the 1970s, American painter Jack Whitten built a 12-foot (3.7- meter) tool he named the “developer” to apply paint to an entire canvas in one motion, resulting in his series of “slab” paintings from that decade. Whitten described this process as making an entire painting in “one gesture,” signaling a clear departure from the prevalence of gestures in his work from the 1960s. Some art historians claim this shift represents “removing gesture” from the process. Therefore, regardless of whether using the developer constitutes a gesture, both Whitten and these art historians likely agree that ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"“Gestures” in painting are typically thought of as bold, expressive brushstrokes. In the 1970s, American painter Jack Whitten built a 12-foot (3.7-","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"meter) tool he named the “developer” to apply paint to an entire canvas in one motion, resulting in his series of “slab” paintings from that decade.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Whitten described this process as making an entire painting in “one gesture,” signaling a clear departure from the prevalence of gestures in his","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"work from the 1960s. Some art historians claim this shift represents “removing gesture” from the process. Therefore, regardless of whether","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"using the developer constitutes a gesture, both Whitten and these art historians likely agree that ______","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice most logically completes the text?","choices":["any tool that a painter uses to create an artwork is capable of creating gestures.","Whitten’s work from the 1960s exhibits many more gestures than his work from the 1970s does.","Whitten became less interested in exploring the role of gesture in his work as his career progressed.","Whitten’s paintings from the 1970s are more realistic than his paintings from the 1960s are."]},{"id":"25893fc7","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Inferences","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Information and Ideas · Inferences","passage":"In many cultures, a handshake can create trust between people. Engineer Jo ão Avelino and his team are designing a robot to shake hands with a human in order to improve human-robot interactions. The robot hand adjusts its movements and pressure to better imitate the feel of a human hand. The researchers want the robot’s handshake to feel realistic because ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In many cultures, a handshake can create trust between people. Engineer João Avelino and his team are designing a robot to shake hands with a","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"human in order to improve human-robot interactions. The robot hand adjusts its movements and pressure to better imitate the feel of a human","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"hand. The researchers want the robot’s handshake to feel realistic because ______","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice most logically completes the text?","choices":["lifelike handshakes may make people more comfortable interacting with robots.","it’s easier to program a robot to perform handshakes than it is to program a robot to perform some other types of greetings.","people are less likely to interact with robots that don’t look like humans.","the robot in the researchers’ study may have uses other than interacting with humans."]},{"id":"409058ee","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Central Ideas and Details","passage":"To protect themselves when being attacked, hagfish —jawless marine animals that resemble eels — will release large quantities of slimy, mucus- like threads. Because these threads are unusually strong and elastic, scientist Atsuko Negishi and her colleagues have been trying to recreate them in a lab as an eco-friendly alternative to petroleum-based fibers that are often used in fabrics. The researchers want to reproduce the threads in the lab because farming hagfish for their slime would be expensive and potentially harmful to the hagfish.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"To protect themselves when being attacked, hagfish—jawless marine animals that resemble eels—will release large quantities of slimy, mucus-","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"like threads. Because these threads are unusually strong and elastic, scientist Atsuko Negishi and her colleagues have been trying to recreate","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"them in a lab as an eco-friendly alternative to petroleum-based fibers that are often used in fabrics. The researchers want to reproduce the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"threads in the lab because farming hagfish for their slime would be expensive and potentially harmful to the hagfish.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best states the text’s main idea?","choices":["The slimy threads that hagfish release might help researchers create a new kind of fabric.","Hagfish have inspired researchers to develop a new petroleum-based fabric.","Hagfish are not well suited to being raised in captivity.","The ability of hagfish to slime their attackers compensates for their being jawless."]},{"id":"f9c4bdab","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"A student is writing a paper about One Night in Miami..., a 2020 film directed by Regina King and written by Kemp Powers. Powers adapted the film’s screenplay from his 2013 play, which he wrote after learning about a 1964 meeting that took place in Miami, Florida, between four prominent figures of the Civil Rights movement: Malcolm X, Muhammad Ali, Jim Brown, and Sam Cooke. The student claims that although Powers was inspired by this meeting, the film is best understood not as a precise retelling of historical events but rather as a largely imagined but informed representation of them.","question":"Which quotation from an article about One Night in Miami... would be the most effective evidence for the student to include in support of this claim?","choices":["“When Powers learned of the meeting, he initially planned to write a much longer work about its four famous participants rather than focusing on the meeting itself.”","“One Night in Miami... received numerous awards and nominations, including an Academy Award nomination for Powers for Best Adapted Screenplay.”","“Powers has described One Night in Miami... as the story of four friends encouraging and supporting one another while engaged in a crucial political debate about how best to achieve equality for Black people in the United States.”","“Powers could find only the most superficial historical details about the meeting, so he read extensively about the four individuals and their thinking at the time in an effort to portray what might have happened between them.”"]},{"id":"6e193b19","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Standard English · Form, Structure, and Sense","passage":"Professional American football player Fred Cox invented one of the world’s most popular toys. In the 1970s, he came up with the idea for the Nerf football, which ______ of the harder and heavier regulation football.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Professional American football player Fred Cox invented one of the world’s most popular toys. In the 1970s, he came up with the idea for the Nerf","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"football, which ______ of the harder and heavier regulation football.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["were a smaller, foam version","are smaller, foam versions","were smaller, foam versions","is a smaller, foam version"]},{"id":"c102f9b0","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Standard English · Form, Structure, and Sense","passage":"Lê Lương Minh became the thirteenth secretary-general of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) in January 2013, making ______ the first time the organization would appoint a Vietnamese leader.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Lê Lương Minh became the thirteenth secretary-general of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) in January 2013, making ______","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"the first time the organization would appoint a Vietnamese leader.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["these","those","this","some"]},{"id":"35ae047d","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Standard English · Form, Structure, and Sense","passage":"In 1929, Edwin Herbert Land invented a polarizing filter that was featured in a number of products, from sunglasses to 3D movies. A decade later, Land ______ his technology to invent the world’s first instant camera, the Polaroid Land camera.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In 1929, Edwin Herbert Land invented a polarizing filter that was featured in a number of products, from sunglasses to 3D movies. A decade later,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Land ______ his technology to invent the world’s first instant camera, the Polaroid Land camera.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["used","to have used","to use","using"]},{"id":"b15724fc","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Boundaries","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Standard English · Boundaries","passage":"American writer Edwidge Danticat, who emigrated from Haiti in 1981, has won acclaim for her powerful short stories, novels, and ______ her lyrical yet unflinching depictions of her native country’s turbulent history, writer Robert Antoni has compared Danticat to Nobel Prize – winning novelist Toni Morrison.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"American writer Edwidge Danticat, who emigrated from Haiti in 1981, has won acclaim for her powerful short stories, novels, and ______ her","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"lyrical yet unflinching depictions of her native country’s turbulent history, writer Robert Antoni has compared Danticat to Nobel Prize–winning","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"novelist Toni Morrison.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["essays, praising","essays and praising","essays praising","essays. Praising"]},{"id":"0bcb4417","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Standard English · Form, Structure, and Sense","passage":"Oglala Lakota poet Layli Long Soldier’s star quilt poems offer an unusually open-ended reading experience. With ______ eight panels of text stitched together in the shape of a traditional eight-pointed Lakota star quilt, the poems present viewers with a seemingly infinite number of ways to read them.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Oglala Lakota poet Layli Long Soldier’s star quilt poems offer an unusually open-ended reading experience. With ______ eight panels of text","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"stitched together in the shape of a traditional eight-pointed Lakota star quilt, the poems present viewers with a seemingly infinite number of","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"ways to read them.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["their","it’s","they’re","its"]},{"id":"e31b0056","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Standard English · Form, Structure, and Sense","passage":"Mary Madden of Ohio ______ a fierce advocate of women’s voting rights in the late 1800s. The dedication of Madden and her fellow activists was rewarded in 1920, when the Nineteenth Amendment to the US Constitution guaranteed American women the right to vote.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Mary Madden of Ohio ______ a fierce advocate of women’s voting rights in the late 1800s. The dedication of Madden and her fellow activists was","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"rewarded in 1920, when the Nineteenth Amendment to the US Constitution guaranteed American women the right to vote.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["are","was","have been","were"]},{"id":"4d2736f0","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"In her poetry collection Thomas and Beulah, Rita Dove interweaves the titular characters personal stories with broader historical narratives. She places Thomas’s journey from the American South to the Midwest in the early 1900s within the larger context of the Great Migration. ______ Dove sets events from Beulah’s personal life against the backdrop of the US Civil Rights Movement.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In her poetry collection Thomas and Beulah, Rita Dove interweaves the titular characters’ personal stories with broader historical narratives. She","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"places Thomas’s journey from the American South to the Midwest in the early 1900s within the larger context of the Great Migration. ______ Dove","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"sets events from Beulah’s personal life against the backdrop of the US Civil Rights Movement.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Specifically,","Thus,","Regardless,","Similarly,"]},{"id":"d2b52c50","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Rhetorical Synthesis","passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes: On January 3, 1959, Alaska became the 49th state to join the US. On August 21, 1959, Hawaii became the 50th state to join the US. A new 50-star US flag was unveiled the same day. The student wants to emphasize the order in which Alaska and Hawaii became US states.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"On January 3, 1959, Alaska became the 49th state to join the US.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"On August 21, 1959, Hawaii became the 50th state to join the US.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"A new 50-star US flag was unveiled the same day.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Alaska, the 49th US state, became a state several months before Hawaii, the 50th state, did.","On August 21, 1959, a new 50-star US flag was unveiled.","The 49th and 50th states to join the US did so in the same year.","The same day that Hawaii became a US state —August 21, 1959 —a new US flag was unveiled."]},{"id":"1773fa73","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Expression of Ideas · Rhetorical Synthesis","passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes: A commodity chain is the series of links connecting the production and purchase of a commodity on the world market. Chinese American anthropologist Anna Tsing studies the contemporary commodity chain of matsutake mushrooms. At one end of the matsutake chain are mushroom pickers in Oregon. At the other end are wealthy consumers who buy the costly matsutake in Japan. According to Tsing, “Japanese traders began importing matsutake in the 1980s, when the scarcity of matsutake in Japan first became clear.” The student wants to provide an overview of the matsutake commodity chain.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"A commodity chain is the series of links connecting the production and purchase of a commodity on the world market.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Chinese American anthropologist Anna Tsing studies the contemporary commodity chain of matsutake mushrooms.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"At one end of the matsutake chain are mushroom pickers in Oregon.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"At the other end are wealthy consumers who buy the costly matsutake in Japan.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"According to Tsing, “Japanese traders began importing matsutake in the 1980s, when the scarcity of matsutake in Japan first became","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"clear.”","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The contemporary matsutake commodity chain has its origins in the 1980s when, according to Tsing, “the scarcity of matsutake in Japan first became clear.”","Commodity chains include the linked production and purchase of commodities, such as the matsutake mushroom, on the world market.","Decades after the Japanese import of matsutake began, a commodity chain now links matsutake pickers in Oregon with wealthy consumers of the costly mushrooms in Japan.","Wealthy consumers who buy the costly mushrooms in Japan are at one end of the matsutake commodity chain."]},{"id":"e2eb70b9","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Expression of Ideas · Rhetorical Synthesis","passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes: Traditionally, manufacturers have dyed denim jeans blue by dipping them in a solution containing indigo powder. Indigo doesn’t dissolve in just water, so manufacturers must mix hazardous chemicals with water to dissolve the powder. Textile researcher Smriti Rai discovered a process for dyeing blue jeans without chemicals. Rai added indigo powder to a hydrogel containing nanocellulose and produced a dye that could be spread directly onto the denim. Nanocellulose is a natural, plant-based substance that separates the molecules of indigo powder. The student wants to emphasize a difference between the two approaches to dyeing blue jeans.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Traditionally, manufacturers have dyed denim jeans blue by dipping them in a solution containing indigo powder.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Indigo doesn’t dissolve in just water, so manufacturers must mix hazardous chemicals with water to dissolve the powder.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Textile researcher Smriti Rai discovered a process for dyeing blue jeans without chemicals.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Rai added indigo powder to a hydrogel containing nanocellulose and produced a dye that could be spread directly onto the denim.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Nanocellulose is a natural, plant-based substance that separates the molecules of indigo powder.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Though created using a different process, Rai’s dye contains the same ingredient as the dye produced by blue jean manufacturers.","Nanocellulose is a natural, plant-based substance that separates the molecules of indigo powder, which doesn’t dissolve in water.","The traditional approach to dyeing blue jeans is to dip them in a solution containing hazardous chemicals.","Rai’s approach substitutes a natural, plant-based substance for the hazardous chemicals that manufacturers have traditionally used."]},{"id":"064c8999","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Rhetorical Synthesis","passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes: The Haber-Bosch process is an industrial process used to manufacture ammonia (NH ). 3 It was invented by chemists Fritz Haber and Carl Bosch in 1910. The process’s primary reaction combines nitrogen (N ) from the air with hydrogen (H ). 2 2 It requires an iron catalyst and high temperatures and pressures. Most of the ammonia produced by this process is used in fertilizers. The student wants to provide an overview of the Haber-Bosch process.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"The Haber-Bosch process is an industrial process used to manufacture ammonia (NH3).","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"It was invented by chemists Fritz Haber and Carl Bosch in 1910.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"The process’s primary reaction combines nitrogen (N2) from the air with hydrogen (H2).","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"It requires an iron catalyst and high temperatures and pressures.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Most of the ammonia produced by this process is used in fertilizers.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Haber-Bosch process needs nitrogen, hydrogen, and an iron catalyst.","The Haber-Bosch process uses an iron catalyst along with high temperatures and pressures to manufacture ammonia from nitrogen and hydrogen.","Chemists Fritz Haber and Carl Bosch invented an industrial process to manufacture ammonia to be used in fertilizers.","In 1910, chemists Fritz Haber and Carl Bosch invented the Haber-Bosch process, which requires high temperatures and pressures."]},{"id":"49fe306b","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Expression of Ideas · Rhetorical Synthesis","passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes: From Earth, all the meteors in a meteor shower appear to originate from a single spot in the sky. This spot is called the meteor shower’s radiant. The Perseid meteor shower is visible in the northern hemisphere in July and August. Like many meteor showers, it is named for the location of its radiant. Its radiant is located within the constellation Perseus. The student wants to explain the origin of the Perseid meteor shower’s name.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"From Earth, all the meteors in a meteor shower appear to originate from a single spot in the sky.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"This spot is called the meteor shower’s radiant.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"The Perseid meteor shower is visible in the northern hemisphere in July and August.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Like many meteor showers, it is named for the location of its radiant.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Its radiant is located within the constellation Perseus.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Perseid meteor shower is named for the constellation Perseus, the location of the meteor shower’s radiant.","A meteor shower’s name may be linked to a single spot in the sky.","The Perseid meteor shower, which has a radiant, is visible in the northern hemisphere in July and August.","From Earth, all the meteors in a meteor shower appear to originate from a radiant, such as the one within Perseus."]}];
